   {
    "t": "IvorySQL_5.6",
    "d": "2026-09-18",
    "n": "PGNexus is now fully compatible with IvorySQL 5.6, bringing a zero-barrier, cloud-based AI-assisted experimentation experience! As a one-stop knowledge and experimentation platform for a wide range of scenarios, PGNexus now supports the latest IvorySQL 5.6. No local installation is required—you can build an environment with one click through the online sandbox. It supports patch application and testing and validation, covering multiple topology architectures including standalone, streaming replication, lo"
   },
   {
    "t": "IvorySQL_1.23",
    "d": "2026-07-27",
    "n": "Support for 7 Additional PostgreSQL Extensions: PostGIS, pgRouting, PGroonga, ddlx, pgsql-http, pgvector, pgvectorscale.\nIvorySQL 1.23, based on PostgreSQL 14.23 and includes a variety of bug fixes.\n- PostgreSQL 14.23 Enhancements\nFor further details, visit link: [PostgreSQL's release notes](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/release/14.23/).\nPostgreSQL kernel upgraded to version 14.23.\n- PostgreSQL Extensions\n- IvorySQL database source code: https://github.com/IvorySQL/IvorySQL"
   },
   {
    "t": "IvorySQL_5.4",
    "d": "2026-06-17",
    "n": "Support for Additional PostgreSQL Extensions and Tools: AGE, ddlx, pg_ai_query, pg_bigm, pg_cron, pg_curl, pg_hint_plan, pg_jieba, pg_partman, pg_show_plans, pg_stat_monitor, pg_textsearch, PgBouncer, pgRouting, pgagent, PGroonga, pgsql-http, pgvector, plpgsql_check, PostGIS, redis_fdw, system_stats, wal2json, Zhparser.\nOffers a fully managed, graphical control plane that handles IvorySQL 5.4 database subscriptions, orchestrates end-to-end lifecycle operations, and integrates surrounding ecosystem services."
   }
  ],
